{"surface": "event", "title": "An AI industry downturn sets in by May 18, 2027", "html": "<div class=\"ev ws\"><div class=\"evh\"><h2 class=\"title\">An AI industry downturn sets in by May 18, 2027</h2><p class=\"facts\"><span>Any time to May 18, 2027</span><span class=\"sep\">·</span><span class=\"src\">Known from Polymarket &#x27;AI bubble burst by...?&#x27; market rules</span></p><div class=\"hds\"><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"definition\"><summary>Definition</summary><div class=\"hdb text\"><p>The AI build-out breaks: by May 18, 2027 the AI industry is in a recognised downturn, as Polymarket&#x27;s &#x27;AI industry downturn&#x27; market defines it (at least three of its six triggers, such as a collapse in GPU rental prices, met within 90 days), rather than a correction in share prices alone.</p></div></details><details class=\"hd\" data-k=\"notes\"><summary>Rationale</summary><div class=\"hdb\"><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:23\" data-note=\"note:23\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"Polymarket asks this downturn by December 31, 2026 and by June 30, 2027 on identical rules (three of six triggers inside 90 days). May 18 falls between; I read the date at a constant daily hazard between the two deadlines, since no scheduled date concentrates the risk.\"><p>Polymarket asks this downturn by December 31, 2026 and by June 30, 2027 on identical rules (three of six triggers inside 90 days). May 18 falls between; I read the date at a constant daily hazard between the two deadlines, since no scheduled date concentrates the risk.</p></div></div><div class=\"note\" data-k=\"note:86\" data-note=\"note:86\"><div class=\"md\" data-md=\"A blockade of or attack on Taiwan would itself meet the downturn market&#x27;s triggers: Nvidia 50% below its record, the semiconductor index 40% below, and TSMC 50% below are three of the six, and my Taiwan row puts all three there.\"><p>A blockade of or attack on Taiwan would itself meet the downturn market&#x27;s triggers: Nvidia 50% below its record, the semiconductor index 40% below, and TSMC 50% below are three of the six, and my Taiwan row puts all three there.</p></div></div></div></details></div></div><div class=\"strip\" data-count=\"6\" style=\"--cols:5\"><div class=\"sf first\" data-k=\"fig:Forecast\"><span class=\"lab\">Forecast</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:2\"><span class=\"n v\">16.9%</span></a></span><a class=\"cap go calc\" data-go=\"x:p:prop:2\">How it’s set →</a></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Market range\"><span class=\"lab\">Market range</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:interval:prop:2\"><span class=\"n v\">7.8%–20.0%</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If Yes\"><span class=\"lab\">If Yes</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:2:yes\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$36,704</span></a></span><span class=\"cap\"><span class=\"n loss\">−7.30%</span> of portfolio</span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:If No\"><span class=\"lab\">If No</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:outcome:prop:2:no\"><span class=\"n v gain\">+$7,456</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Full impact\"><span class=\"lab\">Full impact</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:swing:prop:2\"><span class=\"n v loss\">−$44,160</span></a></span></div><div class=\"sf\" data-k=\"fig:Volatility\"><span class=\"lab\">Volatility</span><span class=\"v\"><a class=\"go num\" data-go=\"x:volatility:prop:2\"><span class=\"n v\">±$16,543</span></a></span></div></div><nav class=\"tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"outcomes\">Outcomes</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"probability\">Probability</button><button type=\"button\" role=\"tab\" data-tab=\"assumptions\">Assumptions</button></nav><section data-pane=\"outcomes\"><div class=\"ev-card po-card\" data-k=\"payoff\"><div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"plab\">P&amp;L by